## Ansible and Debian

Ansible is a separate work, installed by the controller. Debian is a separate
distribution, installed on the target. Neither is redistributed by this
collection. The product uses only `ansible.builtin`; `requirements.yml`
declares no external collection.

The base image `images/base/Containerfile` is built from the Debian minimal
image and Debian packages. Those packages stay under their own licences; the
product neither redistributes modified copies nor relicenses them.

The image installs the Scripts interpreter from its public GitHub release
(`scripts_0.2.1_amd64.deb`, verified against the release `SHA256SUMS`). Scripts
is a separate work under the GPL-3.0-or-later; the image neither redistributes
it as a product nor relicenses it.
